  "notes": "- The display's heartbeat to the management server now also carries the\n  date the display was installed and how long it has been running since it\n  last started. Nothing else is added. Either is left out when the display\n  cannot read it truthfully.\n- The display's heartbeat to the management server now also carries the\n  display's own name (for example ds-91f149) and whether it takes stable or\n  testing updates. Nothing else is added. Either is left out when the\n  display cannot read it truthfully.\n- The display's heartbeat to the management server now also carries the\n  display's address on its own local network (for example 192.168.202.63),\n  so the fleet page can link to its admin page. Only a private local\n  address is ever sent -- never a public internet address. Nothing else is\n  added.",
